From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove@yandex.ru>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:13:30 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: Import from Arc on Windows

Arc for Windows is a packaged app: what macOS keeps in Application
Support/Arc is in its package's folder under %LOCALAPPDATA%\Packages,
laid out the same way, so the sidebar, the profiles and the rest are read
from there.

Its cookies, passwords and cards are encrypted as Chromium does on Windows:
AES-256-GCM with a key kept in "Local State", wrapped by Windows's data
protection for the account (no prompt, unlike the Mac's keychain). Values
under a scheme that can't be read from outside ("v20", a key bound to the
app) are counted as failed instead of being taken for clear text.

While Arc is open nobody else can read its cookie databases on Windows.
The import then says so ("busy") and the tour asks to quit Arc and try
again, rather than bringing the passwords alone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
